What the fork changes
---------------------

New code lives in app/src/main/java/com/limelight/strmqt/ and in resource
files whose names start with "strmqt". Edits to upstream files are kept
small, and are marked "StrmQt fork" where they are code:

- app/build.gradle: the application id (com.strmlight) and name, and JUnit
  for the fork's unit tests.
- app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml: the launcher entry moves from PcView to
  the fork's LaunchActivity; the fork's activities, boot receiver and wake
  service, and the permissions those need.
- app/src/main/java/com/limelight/Game.java: hooks for remote mode and for
  handing an ended stream back to the launcher.
- app/src/main/res/xml/preferences.xml: a "StrmQt" settings category.
- app/src/main/res/mipmap-*/ic_launcher*.png, drawable-xhdpi/atv_banner.png,
  drawable/ic_channel.xml and values/ic_launcher_background.xml: the launcher
  icon and TV banner are replaced with artwork rendered from StrmQt's brand
  files (assets/brand in the StrmQt source). The banner wordmark is set in
  Archivo and IBM Plex Mono, both under the SIL Open Font License.

docs/strmqt-fork.md describes the behaviour, setup and what has been tested.
